0 HEAD
1 GEDC
2 VERS 7.0
1 SOUR EXPORTER
2 VERS 2.1
0 @I1@ INDI
1 NAME Cecil John /Rhodes/
1 SEX M
1 NOTE <p>He was an accountant for Consolidated Gold Fields.</p>
2 MIME text/html
2 LANG en
1 NOTE <p>Declared as HTML and not well formed: the paragraph never closes.
2 MIME text/html
1 NOTE <p>Not declared as anything, so this is a paragraph tag being read as
2 CONT four literal characters followed by a word. Undeclared means text/plain,
2 CONT which makes the markup content rather than markup.</p>
1 NOTE Plain text, said so.
2 MIME text/plain
0 @I2@ INDI
1 NAME Alfred /Beit/
1 SNOTE @N1@
1 NOTE Line breaks are carried by CONT alone in this version.
2 CONT CONC was removed in 7.0, so the 255-character line limit went with it and
2 CONT a payload may simply be as long as it needs to be — this line is longer than
2 CONT any 5.5.1 line was permitted to be, and it is entirely conformant here.
0 @N1@ SNOTE <p>A shared note, which is where 7.0 puts text that many records cite.</p>
1 MIME text/html
1 LANG en
0 TRLR
